reagent-name-fent = fentanyl

reagent-desc-fent = A highly potent, highly addictive opioid painkiller narcotic. When 25 units of Fentanyl is mixed with 1 unit of Tricordrazine and heated to 310k, it crystallizes into a valuable substance. This reaction results in 1 unit of Tricordrazine and 5 units of Dylovene as a byproduct. Because Fentanyl violently explodes with Dylovene, only one crystal can be made at a time.

A highly potent opioid painkiller and narcotic. It is highly addictive, and horribly abused. When mixed with Tricordrazine at a 25:1 ratio (25u Fentanyl, 1u Tricordrazine), and heated to 310k, it is solidified, and highly valuable. Its very explosive with dylovene, and as such you can only crystallize one at a time.

reagent-name-gestalzitine = Gestalzitine
reagent-desc-gestalzitine = An anomalous chemical, not naturally found. It is a highly effective sedative, apparently directly manipulating cerebral functions to force the metabolizer into a dream-like state.
